<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/sound/cae-sound-horizontal-microphone-cockpit.jpg", "Sound measurement equipment" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title" data-i18n="story.0.title">Problem</h2>
      <p class="story__text" data-i18n="story.0.text.0">
        During certification-related work, sound measurements can fall outside expected tolerance with respect to the aircraft test-flight data.
 The challenge was to understand whether the issue came from the setup, acquisition process, environment, or simulator-specific behavior.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text" data-i18n="story.0.text.1">
        The work required a structured approach because audio issues can be hard to troubleshoot:
 small changes in placement, routing, or configuration can change the result.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--reverse">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/sound/cae-sound-measurement-screen.jpg", "Sound measurement inside cockpit" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title" data-i18n="story.1.title">Measurement Workflow</h2>
      <p class="story__text" data-i18n="story.1.text.0">
        I worked through the acquisition chain, comparing measurement conditions, and microphone placement
 and repeatability across multiple simulator platforms, including statistical analysis of the data to identify patterns and potential causes.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text" data-i18n="story.1.text.1">
        The main goal was to narrow the search space and build a clearer troubleshooting sequence
 for future sound measurement issues.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
